WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.175 --> 00:00:04.675
( music)

00:00:07.186 --> 00:00:08.526
- All right, thank you.

00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:10.349
Thanks, Timberley, for the invitation.

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:13.046
In fact when she originally
invited me to submit a proposal

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:16.166
I was thinking, "Well, I
don't know what I do in Canvas

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:18.961
"that is special or is different
from what other people do."

00:00:18.961 --> 00:00:21.479
I've never seen the competition.

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:25.443
I certainly never use quizzes,
or some of these embedding

00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:28.193
of multimedia material on Canvas.

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:33.262
So I really thought hard
about what essentially sums up

00:00:33.262 --> 00:00:35.258
the way that I've been using Canvas,

00:00:35.258 --> 00:00:37.482
and I think it boils down to the way

00:00:37.482 --> 00:00:40.414
that I've used the home
page as the go-to resource

00:00:40.414 --> 00:00:43.055
for a lot of things we do in class.

00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:44.924
So just to give you a bit of background,

00:00:44.924 --> 00:00:46.450
the class I'm showing right here

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.818
is a pretty large statistics class.

00:00:49.818 --> 00:00:52.082
There's about a hundred students,

00:00:52.082 --> 00:00:54.447
and we don't have regular
quizzes and tests,

00:00:54.447 --> 00:00:57.208
we do have two exams
throughout the semester,

00:00:57.208 --> 00:00:59.640
but we do have regular reading assignments

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.632
and homework assignments and so on.

00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:04.291
So, one of the questions
that I'm sure you all have

00:01:04.291 --> 00:01:07.664
from students is, "What's the homework?"

00:01:07.664 --> 00:01:09.174
Or "What's the reading assignment?

00:01:09.174 --> 00:01:12.146
"Where can I find this
that we did in class?"

00:01:12.146 --> 00:01:14.489
And for me, the easiest
way to just put everything

00:01:14.489 --> 00:01:18.412
in a central place has been
to make use of the home page.

00:01:18.412 --> 00:01:22.314
This is just one of the
pages that I've created,

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:25.365
and I clicked to set it as
the home page, and I design it

00:01:25.365 --> 00:01:28.115
to be sort of a growing
syllabus, if you will.

00:01:28.115 --> 00:01:30.840
So initially it'll be week one of class,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.429
and you probably won't
see very much beyond,

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:35.374
say, up to this point.

00:01:35.374 --> 00:01:37.383
So there will be essential information,

00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:39.083
like who are the TAs in the course,

00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:43.019
who are the ULAs, we use
ULAs in this course as well,

00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:46.351
when are their office hours,
and all this is dynamic

00:01:46.351 --> 00:01:48.708
in the sense that we can
change it at any time.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:52.145
It's a website that we can
go in, modify as needed,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:56.333
in order to get the most
up-to-date information.

00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:58.882
So the way that things
progressed is, obviously,

00:01:58.882 --> 00:02:01.244
the important things are way at the top,

00:02:01.244 --> 00:02:03.113
and then I like to organize my material

00:02:03.113 --> 00:02:05.080
on a week to week basis,

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.016
so I try to have a top
level heading per week.

00:02:08.016 --> 00:02:11.768
That's just week one, the date,
what did we cover in class,

00:02:11.768 --> 00:02:15.425
what are the slides that go
along with the material in class

00:02:15.425 --> 00:02:19.083
and what are some computer code examples

00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.136
that would come along with that.

00:02:21.136 --> 00:02:24.237
And I think that this gives
me just a very nice way

00:02:24.237 --> 00:02:26.180
of pointing students to the page.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.247
I can even say things like,
"If you happen to miss class,

00:02:29.247 --> 00:02:31.579
"feel free to just keep
up to date by looking at

00:02:31.579 --> 00:02:33.328
"what's going on on the home page.

00:02:33.328 --> 00:02:36.167
"Everything is posted there,
you wouldn't miss anything."

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.314
The only thing that's
missing is maybe videos

00:02:38.314 --> 00:02:39.993
of our in-class lectures,

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:43.857
but I'm very resistant
against that kind of thing.

00:02:43.857 --> 00:02:46.613
Other things that I
would want to highlight,

00:02:46.613 --> 00:02:49.431
is I did try doing something like this

00:02:49.431 --> 00:02:52.348
with the modules section of Canvas,

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:56.837
and I heard a lot of you use
Canvas very successfully.

00:02:56.837 --> 00:03:00.494
So I do have a slide
example from an earlier,

00:03:00.494 --> 00:03:02.904
a different course where
I did try to implement

00:03:02.904 --> 00:03:06.281
the same kind of thing using modules.

00:03:06.281 --> 00:03:08.036
And I thought this would
make my life easier

00:03:08.036 --> 00:03:09.951
because I could just go ahead and create

00:03:09.951 --> 00:03:12.310
these high level folders
from week to week,

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:15.236
I can include assignments, I
can include any other files

00:03:15.236 --> 00:03:17.750
that I'd like to include normally.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.013
But what I found is that this
is a little less flexible.

00:03:21.013 --> 00:03:24.847
It's much harder for me to
format the names of things

00:03:24.847 --> 00:03:28.412
to include bold facing for
things I'd like to highlight,

00:03:28.412 --> 00:03:30.227
and it takes up a lot of space.

00:03:30.227 --> 00:03:32.462
So week one, for this class for example,

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:34.751
stretches a full page basically.

00:03:34.751 --> 00:03:37.303
I have to scroll down to get to week two.

00:03:37.303 --> 00:03:41.055
Whereas I tend now to prefer
just having everything

00:03:41.055 --> 00:03:43.562
on this home page where
I can even have things

00:03:43.562 --> 00:03:45.490
that are just text, right?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.583
So things like when office hours are,

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:51.781
links to practice exams,
solutions to practice exams.

00:03:51.781 --> 00:03:54.580
Having it all be in that one central place

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.413
seems to me the easiest way to go.

00:03:58.505 --> 00:04:00.442
I guess I still have time remaining.

00:04:00.442 --> 00:04:02.853
So since this is not a
Canvas propaganda session,

00:04:02.853 --> 00:04:04.702
I think I want to also
talk a little bit about

00:04:04.702 --> 00:04:06.791
the struggles that I've had with Canvas,

00:04:06.791 --> 00:04:09.563
if I may, since I have an audience.

00:04:09.563 --> 00:04:12.567
So in my class we have about
four people, five people

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:14.767
grading for every single assignment,

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:18.238
and we do make use of
Canvas’ grading tool.

00:04:18.238 --> 00:04:20.113
I really do like the speed grader,

00:04:20.113 --> 00:04:23.241
that everybody can go in
and see the PDF submissions,

00:04:23.241 --> 00:04:26.446
they can annotate the PDFs,
work with the rubrics,

00:04:26.446 --> 00:04:28.374
and this makes it really easy

00:04:28.374 --> 00:04:30.513
if you don't want people to
be swapping back and forth

00:04:30.513 --> 00:04:33.736
paper assignments, for example.

00:04:33.736 --> 00:04:36.286
One challenge that I've
had, however, is that

00:04:36.286 --> 00:04:39.467
if you have multiple people
grading simultaneously,

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:42.184
the rubric, be very careful,
because they will sometimes

00:04:42.184 --> 00:04:46.072
overwrite each other's
points, and I've had that

00:04:46.072 --> 00:04:48.486
when two graders were
grading simultaneously.

00:04:48.486 --> 00:04:50.332
Someone may be grading problem one,

00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:52.388
someone grading problem five,

00:04:52.388 --> 00:04:54.949
and maybe they're just offset
by a couple of students,

00:04:54.949 --> 00:04:58.575
and somebody will click on
submit and save, and boom,

00:04:58.575 --> 00:05:01.642
the other grade completely
disappears into thin air.

00:05:01.642 --> 00:05:04.027
So I'm hoping that someday
we're able to resolve this.

00:05:04.027 --> 00:05:05.822
I see this as sort of the main complaint

00:05:05.822 --> 00:05:09.096
that I have with Canvas in the meantime.

00:05:09.096 --> 00:05:11.284
But otherwise, I think
the students have been

00:05:11.284 --> 00:05:13.519
fairly satisfied with being able to have

00:05:13.519 --> 00:05:15.519
everything in one place.

00:05:17.982 --> 00:05:19.649
Sorry about that.

00:05:19.649 --> 00:05:23.446
And being able to see their
grades, see their feedback,

00:05:23.446 --> 00:05:25.521
and being able to submit
things very easily

00:05:25.521 --> 00:05:28.831
without having to appear in
person to turn things in.

00:05:28.831 --> 00:05:30.331
That's all I have.

00:05:31.535 --> 00:05:34.535
(audience applauds)

00:05:37.306 --> 00:05:39.393
- [Audience Member] So,
the grading challenge,

00:05:39.393 --> 00:05:40.943
I don't know if I understood you clearly.

00:05:40.943 --> 00:05:44.361
So presume two teaching fellows
are grading simultaneously

00:05:44.361 --> 00:05:45.898
the same assignment.
- Exactly.

00:05:45.898 --> 00:05:47.849
- [Audience Member] They
would be doing it why?

00:05:47.849 --> 00:05:50.027
Is it accidental, or
you deliberately assign,

00:05:50.027 --> 00:05:53.586
like, the TF one will
grade problems one to two,

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:56.947
and TF two will grade
problems three to four.

00:05:56.947 --> 00:05:59.129
I mean, why would that problem occur?

00:05:59.129 --> 00:06:00.262
- That's a very good question.

00:06:00.262 --> 00:06:02.641
So, in my mind, because we want

00:06:02.641 --> 00:06:06.384
to have our ULAs and
TAs grade consistently,

00:06:06.384 --> 00:06:09.740
we want to, instead of having
them grade different students,

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.770
maybe they just grade different problems.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:15.889
That way everybody, one TF
will grade all of problem one,

00:06:15.889 --> 00:06:18.559
one TF will grade all of problem two,

00:06:18.559 --> 00:06:20.675
and so in that case it is
possible for two of them

00:06:20.675 --> 00:06:24.425
to be grading the same
person simultaneously.

00:06:29.302 --> 00:06:30.838
- [Audience Member] Can you
set it so that the students

00:06:30.838 --> 00:06:35.838
receive an email announcement
when you update the home page?

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.071
- I have not figured out how to do that.

00:06:38.071 --> 00:06:41.784
That would certainly be ideal, yeah.

00:06:41.784 --> 00:06:44.878
- [Audience Member] I think
there might be a notify users

00:06:44.878 --> 00:06:46.617
that an update has been made,

00:06:46.617 --> 00:06:48.820
at the bottom of the page
before you hit submit.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:52.425
- Ah. I should look into
that, I think that would be

00:06:52.425 --> 00:06:55.212
an excellent sort of improvement
upon the current system

00:06:55.212 --> 00:06:58.189
to have students see that
new material has been posted.

00:06:58.189 --> 00:06:59.953
- [Audience Member] I
don't think that happens

00:06:59.953 --> 00:07:01.185
on pages, unfortunately.

00:07:01.185 --> 00:07:03.006
It is assignments, you
can do it for assignments

00:07:03.006 --> 00:07:04.371
but not on pages right now.

00:07:04.371 --> 00:07:08.038
- Okay. Someday.
(laughter)

00:07:10.403 --> 00:07:12.110
Thank you very much.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.450
- [Audience Member] Thank you.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.700
(applause)

00:07:18.613 --> 00:07:22.030
(gentle xylophone music)

